title The section that wanted a shelf
prompt Keaton -- fold the product direction section, store it to a file and fascia connect to it
think Read the section before cutting it and found it was TWO things braided: a dozen lines of genuine product direction -- Linengrow, Dimeroll, Tally, Mantra, the product cards -- and then a long run of per-ship landed accounts.
think Only the second wants a shelf. Folding the whole section would have taken the direction off the card along with the receipts, which is the opposite of what a live front is for.
obs The move is established rather than invented: construction/archive/ already holds 451 shelves named itinerary-landed-accounts, so the fold reuses that name and that shape.
obs THE MOVED TEXT CARRIED LINKS WRITTEN AT THE CARD'S DEPTH. Twenty-two of them broke the moment the bytes sat one directory lower -- every archive/X became a sibling X and every ../Y needed ../../Y. Repaired the body and left my own header links alone, since those were written for the new depth already.
obs The prior shelf I checked carries no relative links at all, so nothing in the room had taught this yet. The link scan reads it as outside the tree until the file is STAGED, which is the reading that found the last one.
obs WITHDREW MY OWN BOUND RAISE IN THE SAME LAP. I raised the card to 49152 an hour ago because it stood 39 bytes under its ceiling; the fold took it from 41,230 to 19,964, so the raise stopped being earned and went back to 40960. A bound that only falls is the one worth having.
obs SURFACED RATHER THAN FIXED: construction/archive/ holds 975 flat entries against a 256 bound, and sits 25 entries under GitHub's 1,000-entry listing cliff. That is the one room readme_metrics reports over bound. A 975-file day-fold is its own lap and its own word.
loom card bytes_before=41230 bytes_after=19964 max=40960 headroom=20996 sections=12
loom fold shelf_bytes=22404 links_repointed=22 links_broken_after=0 room_flat_entries=975 room_bound=256
rota lap 4559, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in: take in the concrete fact at the door. What it surfaced: the section was two things, and the door told me so before any argument about where it should go.
file construction/ITINERARY.md the landed accounts replaced by one pointer, the bound raise withdrawn
file construction/archive/20260915-180554_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the shelf, links repointed to its depth
file context/specs/20260724-132812_pin-and-ledger-living-pin-max-bytes.md the raise withdrawn at its one declaration
scope one card section folded to a shelf, its links repointed, the bound raise withdrawn, one room named as over bound
